  <Sequence DisplayName="Scheduling Bot - Main" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_1">
    <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>SCHEDULING BOT — queue-driven performer.

Implements docs/phase2/bot_scheduling.md. Build the activity tree inside each
stage below; the stages, their order and the guards are the design and must not
be rearranged without changing that document first.

TRANSACTION SHAPE (REFramework):
  Init -> GetTransactionItem -> Process -> SetTransactionStatus -> loop

THE THREE GUARDS AGAINST DOUBLE-BOOKING (all three are required):
  1. POST /api/v1/slots/{id}/lock          120s TTL
  2. GET  /api/v1/slots/{id}               re-check status AND version
  3. Partial unique index in the HMS       last line of defence

The lock release in the Finally block is mandatory. A crashed transaction that
keeps its lock silently degrades the next two minutes of bookings.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
    <Sequence.Variables>
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Object" Name="TransactionItem" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="scg:Dictionary(x:String, x:Object)" Name="Config" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtRules" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="sd:DataTable" Name="dtSlots" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="TransactionNumber" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="AttemptsUsed" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="PatientId" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="SelectedSlotId" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="SelectedSlotVersion" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Int32" Name="AllocationPass" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:String" Name="Priority" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:String" Name="ReferenceNo" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:String" Name="ErrorCode" />
      <Variable x:TypeArguments="x:Boolean" Name="HasSlot" />
    </Sequence.Variables>

    <ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log - Start" Level="Info"
      Message="&quot;SchedulingBot starting. Queue: &quot; &amp; in_QueueName"
      sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_1" />

    <Sequence DisplayName="1. Initialisation" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_2">
      <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>1. INITIALISATION — Workflows/InitAllSettings.xaml + InitAllApplications.xaml

  a. Read Data/Config.xlsx -> Config dictionary
  b. Read Data/rules.xlsx  -> dtRules (generated by tools/yaml_to_xlsx.py)
  c. Get Orchestrator assets: HMS_BaseUrl, HMS_ApiKey, Twilio_*, SendGrid_*,
     Excel_FilePath, MaxRetryAttempts, DryRunNotifications
  d. Open the browser at Config("HMS_BaseUrl") and log in

  Any failure here is a SYSTEM exception — stop the job rather than failing
  transactions one at a time against a broken environment.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
      <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke InitAllSettings.xaml and InitAllApplications.xaml"
        sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_1" />
    </Sequence>

    <While DisplayName="2. Transaction loop" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="While_1"
      Condition="[TransactionNumber &lt; in_MaxTransactions]">
      <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>2. TRANSACTION LOOP

Get Transaction Item from the BookingRequests queue. Exit when it returns
Nothing (queue empty) or in_MaxTransactions is reached.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
      <Sequence DisplayName="Transaction" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_3">

        <Sequence DisplayName="2a. Get transaction item" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_4">
          <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Get Transaction Item (QueueName: in_QueueName).
If TransactionItem Is Nothing -> Break out of the loop; the queue is empty.

SpecificContent fields:
  RequestId, PatientName, Phone, Email, Department, PreferredDoctor,
  PreferredDateFrom, PreferredDateTo, TimeBand, Urgency, IsFollowUp, Reason</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
          <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Get Transaction Item -> TransactionItem"
            sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_2" />
        </Sequence>

        <TryCatch DisplayName="2b. Process transaction" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_1">
          <TryCatch.Try>
            <Sequence DisplayName="Process" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_5">

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 1 - Validate request" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_6">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Validate the queue item before touching the HMS.
  Phone matches ^\+[1-9]\d{9,14}$ , dates present and not reversed,
  department known, urgency in NORMAL/HIGH/URGENT.

Invalid -> throw BusinessRuleException("VALIDATION_ERROR").
NEVER retried: retrying a malformed phone number three times just burns
capacity and still fails.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): validate SpecificContent fields"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_3" />
              </Sequence>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 2 - Lookup or register patient" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_7">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/LookupOrRegisterPatient.xaml — UI AUTOMATION.

  Navigate /admin/patients
  Type Into  [data-automation-id='pat-search-input']  &lt;- Phone (the dedup key)
  Click      [data-automation-id='pat-search-btn']
  If element [data-automation-id='pat-no-results'] exists:
      Click  [data-automation-id='pat-new-btn']
      Fill   pat-new-name / pat-new-phone / pat-new-email / pat-new-dob
      Click  [data-automation-id='pat-new-save']
      Scrape [data-automation-id='pat-new-id'] -> PatientId
  Else:
      Scrape first [data-automation-id='pat-row-id'] -> PatientId

Search is by phone and never by name: name matching must not auto-merge
records, which is what creates duplicates in the manual process.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke LookupOrRegisterPatient.xaml -> PatientId"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_4" />
              </Sequence>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 3 - Derive priority" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_8">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>rules.yaml priority.derivation — first match wins:
  Urgency = URGENT            -> URGENT
  Urgency = HIGH              -> HIGH
  Patient age &gt;= 60          -> HIGH
  IsFollowUp = True           -> HIGH
  otherwise                   -> NORMAL

Run this BEFORE allocation: priority decides whether emergency-reserve
slots are even eligible.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Assign Priority from the rules above"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_5" />
              </Sequence>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 4 - Scrape schedule" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_9">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/ScrapeDoctorSchedule.xaml — UI AUTOMATION.

  Navigate /admin/schedule
  Select sch-department, sch-doctor, sch-date-from, sch-date-to, sch-status
  Click  sch-load-btn
  Table Extraction on [data-automation-id='sch-slot-table'] -> dtSlots

Columns returned in fixed order:
  SlotId, DoctorId, DoctorName, Department, Date, StartTime, EndTime,
  Status, IsEmergencyReserve, Version

If [data-automation-id='sch-no-slots'] exists -> HasSlot = False.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke ScrapeDoctorSchedule.xaml -> dtSlots"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_6" />
              </Sequence>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 5 - Allocate slot" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_10">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/AllocateSlot.xaml — PURE LOGIC, NO UI.

Keep this workflow free of UI activities. DataTable in, SlotId out. That is
what makes the Phase 4 edge-case tests runnable without a browser.

ELIGIBILITY FILTER (applied to every pass):
  Status = AVAILABLE, SlotId not in ExcludedSlotIds, Date in window,
  doctor active, (not emergency reserve OR Priority = URGENT),
  doctor daily count &lt; cap, department daily count &lt; cap,
  start &gt;= Now + min_booking_lead_hours.

FOUR PASSES, in order — the first that yields a candidate wins:
  1. Preferred doctor + preferred time band
  2. Preferred doctor, any time
  3. Any doctor in department + preferred time band
  4. Any doctor, any time (first-fit fallback)

SCORING WITHIN A PASS (weights from dtRules):
  weight_earliest        * (horizon - daysOut)
  weight_urgency_boost   * (horizon - daysOut)   if Priority = URGENT
  weight_time_band_match if the band matches
  weight_preferred_doctor if the doctor matches
  weight_load_balance    * (1 - doctorLoad)
  weight_contiguity      if adjacent to an existing booking

  Order by Score DESC, Date ASC, StartTime ASC, SlotId ASC.
  The final SlotId tie-break is what makes two runs over the same data pick
  the same slot — without it the Phase 4 tests are not reproducible.

No candidate in any pass -> BusinessRuleException("NO_SLOT_AVAILABLE").</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke AllocateSlot.xaml -> SelectedSlotId, AllocationPass"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_7" />
              </Sequence>

              <TryCatch DisplayName="Step 6 - Lock, re-check and book" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_2">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>THE CRITICAL SECTION. Guards 1 and 2 live here; guard 3 is the HMS index.

  a. POST /api/v1/slots/{SelectedSlotId}/lock   body {"locked_by":"SchedulingBot"}
       error SLOT_LOCKED  -> retry with the next-best slot
  b. GET  /api/v1/slots/{SelectedSlotId}
       status &lt;&gt; AVAILABLE OR version &lt;&gt; SelectedSlotVersion
                          -> retry with the next-best slot
  c. Navigate /admin/book, fill book-patient-id, book-slot-id, book-priority,
     book-reason, book-is-followup, book-queue-ref; click book-submit
  d. If [data-automation-id='book-success'] exists:
         scrape book-reference-no -> ReferenceNo
     Else:
         scrape book-error-code -> ErrorCode

  Retryable error codes: SLOT_TAKEN, SLOT_LOCKED  (max 3 attempts, then
  BusinessRuleException "SLOT_CONTENTION")
  Non-retryable: VALIDATION_ERROR, DAILY_CAP_REACHED, DOCTOR_INACTIVE,
  PATIENT_NOT_FOUND, SLOT_BLOCKED</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <TryCatch.Try>
                  <Sequence DisplayName="Lock - recheck - submit" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_11">
                    <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): lock slot, re-check version, fill and submit the booking form"
                      sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_8" />
                  </Sequence>
                </TryCatch.Try>
                <TryCatch.Finally>
                  <Sequence DisplayName="Always release the lock" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_12">
                    <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>MANDATORY. POST /api/v1/slots/{SelectedSlotId}/release

Runs whether the booking succeeded, failed or threw. A crashed transaction
that keeps its lock makes the next 120 seconds of bookings silently worse.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                    <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): POST /api/v1/slots/{SelectedSlotId}/release"
                      sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_9" />
                  </Sequence>
                </TryCatch.Finally>
              </TryCatch>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 7 - Mirror to Excel" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_13">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/MirrorToExcel.xaml

Append one row to Config("Excel_FilePath"), sheet "Appointments":
  ReferenceNo, PatientMRN, PatientName, Phone, Department, DoctorName,
  AppointmentDate, AppointmentTime, Status, Priority, BookedBy, SyncedAt

Then PATCH /api/v1/appointments/{id} {"synced_to_excel_at": true}.

Part of the same transaction as the booking, which is how the duplicate
data entry from the manual process stops being a separate human task.
EXCEL_FILE_LOCKED is a SYSTEM exception — a human has the file open.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke MirrorToExcel.xaml"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_10" />
              </Sequence>

              <Sequence DisplayName="Step 8 - Send confirmation" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_14">
                <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/SendConfirmation.xaml -> shared/SendSMS.xaml or SendEmail.xaml

Channel per rules.yaml reminders.channel and the patient's consent flags.
Template TPL_CONFIRMATION_EN. Then POST /api/v1/notifications to log it.

If Config("DryRunNotifications") is True, log the message and record the
notification with provider = DRYRUN instead of sending. Phase 4 batch tests
run this way so they do not burn the Twilio trial credit.

A failed confirmation does NOT fail the transaction: the appointment is
booked, and that is the outcome that matters. Log it and continue.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Invoke SendConfirmation.xaml"
                  sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_11" />
              </Sequence>

            </Sequence>
          </TryCatch.Try>
          <TryCatch.Catches>
            <Catch x:TypeArguments="ui:BusinessRuleException"
              sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Catch_1">
              <ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="ui:BusinessRuleException">
                <ActivityAction.Argument>
                  <DelegateInArgument x:TypeArguments="ui:BusinessRuleException" Name="bex" />
                </ActivityAction.Argument>
                <Sequence DisplayName="Business exception" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_15">
                  <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>BUSINESS EXCEPTION — the process said no. NEVER retried.

Set Transaction Status = Failed, ErrorType = Business, with the reason code.
Orchestrator will not re-queue it; it goes to the exception queue for a clerk.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                  <ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log business exception" Level="Warn"
                    Message="[&quot;Business exception: &quot; &amp; bex.Message]"
                    sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_2" />
                </Sequence>
              </ActivityAction>
            </Catch>
            <Catch x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Private.CoreLib"
              sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Catch_2">
              <ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Private.CoreLib">
                <ActivityAction.Argument>
                  <DelegateInArgument x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" Name="ex"
                    xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Private.CoreLib" />
                </ActivityAction.Argument>
                <Sequence DisplayName="System exception" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_16">
                  <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>SYSTEM EXCEPTION — the environment failed. Orchestrator retries it.

Take a screenshot, close and reopen the browser, set Transaction Status =
Failed with ErrorType = Application so the item is re-queued.

Getting this split backwards is the classic REFramework mistake: a business
failure retried three times wastes capacity and still fails, and a system
failure not retried loses work that would have succeeded on the second try.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
                  <ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log system exception" Level="Error"
                    Message="[&quot;System exception: &quot; &amp; ex.Message]"
                    sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_3" />
                </Sequence>
              </ActivityAction>
            </Catch>
          </TryCatch.Catches>
        </TryCatch>

        <Sequence DisplayName="2c. Set transaction status" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_17">
          <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Set Transaction Status.

On success, attach output data so the run is auditable afterwards:
  AppointmentId, ReferenceNo, SlotId, DoctorId, DoctorName,
  AppointmentDateTime, AllocationPass, AttemptsUsed,
  NotificationChannel, ExcelSynced

AllocationPass and AttemptsUsed are logged deliberately — they are what tell
the Phase 4 report how often a patient got their preferred doctor rather
than a fallback.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
          <ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): Set Transaction Status with output data"
            sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_12" />
        </Sequence>

        <Assign DisplayName="Increment counter" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Assign_1">
          <Assign.To>
            <OutArgument x:TypeArguments="x:Int32">[TransactionNumber]</OutArgument>
          </Assign.To>
          <Assign.Value>
            <InArgument x:TypeArguments="x:Int32">[TransactionNumber + 1]</InArgument>
          </Assign.Value>
        </Assign>
      </Sequence>
    </While>

    <Sequence DisplayName="3. Close applications" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_18">
      <sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Workflows/CloseAllApplications.xaml — close the browser, release any held
locks, write the run summary to the Orchestrator log.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
      <ui:LogMessage DisplayName="Log - Finished" Level="Info"
        Message="[&quot;SchedulingBot finished. Processed: &quot; &amp; TransactionNumber.ToString()]"
        sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="LogMessage_4" />
    </Sequence>
  </Sequence>
</Activity>
